WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.140
Heads move during a brain scan, even when people try hard to stay still.

2
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.682
And when that happens, the PET image and the MR image stop lining up.

3
00:00:10.132 --> 00:00:16.942
Most correction methods compare how bright the two images are. They don't use what the tracer does in each kind of tissue.

4
00:00:17.392 --> 00:00:24.099
Our idea starts with white matter. Amyloid tracers bind there at a high, steady level, so it makes a clean target.

5
00:00:24.549 --> 00:00:33.142
So we take the white matter mask from the MR and slide it over the PET. The best spot is where the average uptake inside the mask is highest.

6
00:00:33.592 --> 00:00:39.810
A search routine called Nelder-Mead does the sliding for us. It starts from 100 random guesses.

7
00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:45.652
Then we apply that same move to the MR and its masks. Everything lines up again.

8
00:00:46.002 --> 00:00:49.689
Want to try it? Drag the mask in the demo below.

